course: dictionary
lesson: 14512
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right. Peppermint can name a plant, a flavour, or a sweet.
explain: «Grandma made a cup of peppermint tea after dinner.» Here peppermint is the flavour in the tea. Ask yourself: what does the drink taste of? The word «tea» is your clue.
explain: «The sweet shop sold peppermints in little paper bags.» The s on peppermints shows you can count them, like sweets in a bag. So here it means a sweet with that fresh, minty flavour.
fact: Peppermint is a mint plant with a strong, fresh, cool taste and smell.
fact: Peppermint can also mean the flavour or oil from this plant, as in «peppermint tea» or «peppermint oil».
fact: A peppermint is a sweet with this flavour, and you can have «a packet of peppermints».
fact: The oil makes your mouth feel cold because a chemical called menthol tricks the nerves.
exercise: «The garden had rows of mint and peppermint plants.» What is a peppermint plant? | A kind of bird | A tall tree in a forest | A grey stone | *A plant with a strong, fresh, cool smell
exercise: Dad says, «This toothpaste has a peppermint flavour.» What does peppermint mean here? | A plant growing in the garden | A loud noise | A bowl for soup | *The fresh, cool taste
exercise: «Can I have a peppermint from the jar, please?» What is a peppermint here? | A toy for a dog | A drink made from milk | *A small sweet with a minty flavour | A cup of hot water
test: «I love the taste of peppermint in my toothpaste.» What does peppermint mean in this sentence? | A box for keeping sweets | A kind of cold drink | A green leaf picked from a bush | *The fresh, minty flavour
test: Which phrase is a sweet, not a drink or an oil? | peppermint oil | *a peppermint | peppermint tea
exam: Why does peppermint oil make your mouth feel cold? | It is always kept in the fridge | It has ice mixed into it | Peppermint is a cold colour | *A chemical called menthol tricks the nerves in your mouth
